## What it does
```text
recruiter> Find me a Junior Data Analyst who knows SQL and Tableau
Understood requirements: skill: SQL, skill: Tableau, role: data analyst, experience: up to 2 years

#1  Amna Rossi (R0013)  - Junior Data Analyst, 1y   coverage 100%
    skills matched: SQL, Tableau   missing: -
    why [A, fit 5/5]: Role: Junior Data Analyst, 1 year of experience. Meets SQL; Tableau; ...
      evidence: "Skills: Excel, Statistics, Python, Power BI, ETL, SQL, Tableau, ..."
#2  ...   coverage 75%   missing: SQL
```
(Real output from the bundled **synthetic** sample - fictional people - using the offline template explainer; shortened.)

1. **Retrieve** - resumes are chunked (section-aware + a structured profile chunk), embedded and stored in FAISS or ChromaDB; search is dense, BM25 or **hybrid (reciprocal-rank fusion)**.
2. **Understand the request** - requested skills, seniority ("junior"), years ("3-5 years") and role are parsed; every candidate gets a **requirement coverage** and the list can be re-ranked by it.
3. **Explain** - the top 3 are sent to an LLM, which writes why each fits, what is missing, and quotes the evidence; every quote is **verified against the resume text**.
4. **Stay fair and private** - names, contact data, pronouns and personal-detail lines are redacted before embedding and before any LLM call; a **bias audit** tests whether gendered cues change the ranking.

## Task checklist
| Requirement from the brief | Where |
|---|---|
| Dataset: Resume Entities for NER (Kaggle) | `data.py` parses the Kaggle annotation format (+ CSV / txt folders) · [`docs/DATASET.md`](docs/DATASET.md) |
| RAG pipeline: embed resumes into a **vector database** (ChromaDB or FAISS) | `index.py`, `stores.py`: **both** FAISS and ChromaDB (+ NumPy), identical results verified by tests |
| Semantic search that retrieves candidates from natural-language queries | `TalentIndex.search` / `TalentSearch.search` - dense, BM25, hybrid |
| **LLM-based evaluation**: top 3 resumes to an LLM (Llama 3 / GPT) for a text summary of why they fit | `explain.py`, `llm.py`: OpenAI-compatible, **Gemini**, **Ollama (Llama 3)**; offline template fallback |
| Tools: LangChain / LlamaIndex | `langchain_adapter.py` (`TalentRetriever`, a standard LangChain retriever) |
| Tools: Hugging Face Transformers | `HFEmbedder` (MiniLM, BGE, E5 or any encoder) |
| Tools: OpenAI / Gemini API | `OpenAICompatibleClient`, `GeminiClient` (standard-library HTTP, no SDK needed) |
| Bonus: **Bias check** that flags demographic favouritism | `bias.py`: counterfactual test + qualified-selection parity · `bias-audit` command |
| Bonus: **Streamlit** chat UI | `app/streamlit_app.py` |

## Architecture
```mermaid
flowchart LR
    R[Resumes<br/>Kaggle JSON / CSV / txt] --> A[anonymise<br/>name · e-mail · phone · pronouns · DOB ...]
    A --> C[chunk<br/>sections + profile chunk]
    C --> E[embed<br/>LSA offline · MiniLM · BGE · E5]
    E --> V[(vector store<br/>FAISS · ChromaDB · NumPy)]
    C --> B[BM25]
    Q[Recruiter query] --> P[parse<br/>skills · years · role]
    Q --> S[dense search + BM25]
    V --> S
    B --> S
    S --> F[reciprocal-rank fusion<br/>+ requirement re-ranking]
    P --> F
    F --> T[top-3 + evidence]
    T --> L[LLM explanation<br/>Llama 3 / GPT / Gemini / template]
    L --> G[grounding check<br/>quotes verified]
    G --> O[answer: candidates, why, gaps]
    F --> U[bias audit]
```
Details: [`docs/METHODOLOGY.md`](docs/METHODOLOGY.md).

## Quick start
```bash
git clone https://github.com/salikhussain71-code/rag-talent-search-engine.git
cd rag-talent-search-engine

python -m venv .venv
# Windows (PowerShell):  .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1      Windows (cmd): .venv\Scripts\activate.bat
# Linux / macOS:         source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -e ".[dev]"            # FAISS, ChromaDB, LangChain core, Streamlit, torch + transformers, pytest, ruff
python -m talent_rag demo          # offline end-to-end run on the bundled synthetic sample (a few seconds)
streamlit run app/streamlit_app.py # chat UI (loads outputs/demo/index created by the demo)
```
The demo needs **no internet and no API key**: it uses offline LSA embeddings and the template explainer.
Lighter install (no torch / chroma): `pip install -e ".[faiss]"` then use `--store faiss` or `--store numpy`.

## Usage
```bash
# 0. Get the real data (docs/DATASET.md) and look at it
python -m talent_rag stats --data "data/raw/Entity Recognition in Resumes.json"

# 1. Build the index (real semantic embeddings; downloads the model once)
python -m talent_rag build-index --data "data/raw/Entity Recognition in Resumes.json" --out outputs/kaggle_index --embedder bge-small --store faiss
#    embedders: lsa (offline) | minilm | bge-small | e5-small | hf:<hub id or folder>      stores: faiss | chroma | numpy

# 2. Search
python -m talent_rag search "Find me a Junior Data Analyst who knows SQL and Tableau" --index outputs/kaggle_index
python -m talent_rag search "Senior DevOps engineer, 6+ years, AWS and Kubernetes" --index outputs/kaggle_index --mode hybrid -k 5 --json
python -m talent_rag chat --index outputs/kaggle_index                # interactive terminal chat

# 3. Evaluate retrieval (annotation-derived benchmark) and audit bias
python -m talent_rag evaluate  --data "data/raw/Entity Recognition in Resumes.json" --embedders lsa minilm bge-small --compare-anonymization
python -m talent_rag bias-audit --data "data/raw/Entity Recognition in Resumes.json" --embedder bge-small
```
From Python:
```python
from talent_rag.index import TalentIndex
from talent_rag.searcher import TalentSearch

index = TalentIndex.load("outputs/kaggle_index")
result = TalentSearch(index).search("Junior Data Analyst who knows SQL and Tableau", k=3, explain=True)
for hit, cov in zip(result.hits, result.coverages):
    print(hit.rank, hit.resume.name, hit.resume.title, f"{cov.score:.0%}", cov.missing_skills)
print(result.explanation.overall)
```

## LLM explanations
| `--explain` value | Backend |
|---|---|
| `template` (default) / `none` | offline deterministic explainer (no LLM) / no explanation |
| `ollama:llama3.1:8b` | **Llama 3 running locally** through Ollama - recommended for real resumes |
| `openai:gpt-4o-mini` | OpenAI (or any OpenAI-compatible server via `OPENAI_BASE_URL`) |
| `gemini:gemini-2.5-flash` | Google Gemini |

Setup, API keys, model names and troubleshooting: [`docs/LLM_SETUP.md`](docs/LLM_SETUP.md). Model names change often - use the one in your provider's docs.
If the LLM is unreachable or answers with invalid JSON, the engine **falls back to the template explainer and tells you why**.

## Bonus features
* **Bias check** - `python -m talent_rag bias-audit`: (1) *counterfactual test* - every gender-coded candidate is rewritten with the counterpart name, e-mail and
  swapped pronouns, the same queries are run on both versions and rankings/scores are compared; (2) *qualified-selection parity* - selection rate of each group among qualified
  candidates with the disparate-impact ratio and a Fisher exact test. Anonymisation ON must give **exactly zero** change (verified in the tests).
* **Streamlit chat UI** - `streamlit run app/streamlit_app.py`: chat history, candidate cards with coverage, evidence snippets, explanation, grounding warnings, sidebar settings
  (mode, k, re-ranking weight, LLM backend), "Show names" toggle.
* **Hybrid retrieval, requirement-aware re-ranking, grounded explanations, LangChain retriever** (`from talent_rag.langchain_adapter import TalentRetriever`).

## Results

### Smoke test on the bundled synthetic sample (45 resumes)
> ⚠️ **Not a benchmark.** The sample is small, easy and synthetic; nearly every configuration scores close to perfect, BM25 is favoured because relevance is defined by
> skill mentions, and re-ranking by requirement coverage looks perfect *by construction* (the benchmark's relevance rule is the same check). The numbers only prove the pipeline works.

Bias audit on the sample (30 queries): with anonymisation **ON**, swapping gendered names/pronouns changed nothing (top-3 overlap 1.000, max score change 0.0000); with
anonymisation **OFF** it changed the top-3 for 1 of 30 queries (3%, max score change 0.053). Full tables: [`outputs/demo/`](outputs/demo/).

### Real Kaggle data (fill in after your runs)
```bash
python -m talent_rag evaluate --data "data/raw/Entity Recognition in Resumes.json" --embedders lsa minilm bge-small --compare-anonymization --out outputs/kaggle_evaluation
```
| embedder | mode | anonymised | precision@3 | MRR | nDCG@10 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| *(run the command above and paste outputs/kaggle_evaluation/retrieval_report.md)* | | | | | |

> No real-data numbers are claimed here: the environment this project was written in has no access to Kaggle, the Hugging Face hub or LLM APIs.

## Verification status
What was actually tested (129 automated tests, all passing; Python 3.12; CPU):

| Area | How it was verified |
|---|---|
| Kaggle format parsing, offsets, CSV / folder inputs, robustness | unit tests incl. inclusive / exclusive `end`, null annotations, duplicate ids |
| Anonymisation | tests for e-mail / phone / URL / names / pronouns / titles / personal-detail lines (whole-line and inline); job terms are kept; a job title on line 1 is *not* mistaken for a name |
| FAISS, **ChromaDB**, NumPy stores | real libraries; identical top-k rankings, k clamping, extension, save/load and persistence |
| Hugging Face embedder code path | pooling, prefixes, batching, determinism with a tiny local BERT |
| Dense / BM25 / hybrid search, re-ranking, evidence | integration tests; hybrid score equals the RRF formula |
| **LLM clients** (OpenAI-compatible, Gemini, Ollama) | tested against a **real local HTTP server**: request path, headers, payload, response parsing, retries, error handling, API key never leaked |
| Explanation grounding | hallucinated quotes flagged, invalid JSON / LLM failure fall back to the template, prompt contains no names / e-mails / ids |
| Bias audit | exact zero change with anonymisation on; non-zero without; counts add up; small-sample warning |
| Streamlit chat UI, CLI, LangChain retriever | `streamlit.testing`, CLI tests (all commands + error paths), retriever test |

**Not tested here** (no internet, hub or API access): downloading real embedding models (MiniLM / BGE / E5), calls to the real OpenAI / Gemini / Ollama services,
the real Kaggle file, and retrieval quality with real semantic embeddings. The code paths around them are covered by the tests above; the request formats follow the providers' documented REST APIs.

## Project structure
```
rag-talent-search-engine/
├── src/talent_rag/
│   ├── data.py          # Kaggle / CSV / txt loaders, entities, years of experience, skill splitting
│   ├── anonymize.py     # PII + protected-characteristic redaction
│   ├── chunking.py      # section-aware chunks + profile chunk
│   ├── embedders.py     # LSA (offline) and Hugging Face encoders
│   ├── stores.py        # NumPy / FAISS / ChromaDB vector stores
│   ├── bm25.py          # Okapi BM25
│   ├── index.py         # TalentIndex: build / save / load / dense-BM25-hybrid search
│   ├── query.py         # skill vocabulary, query parsing, requirement coverage
│   ├── searcher.py      # search + coverage + re-ranking + explanation
│   ├── llm.py           # OpenAI-compatible / Gemini / Ollama clients (stdlib HTTP)
│   ├── explain.py       # grounded explanations, quote verification, template fallback
│   ├── evaluate.py      # annotation-derived benchmark, metrics, configuration comparison
│   ├── bias.py          # counterfactual + parity audit
│   ├── langchain_adapter.py
│   ├── visualize.py · testing.py · lexicons.py · config.py
│   └── cli.py           # python -m talent_rag {info,stats,build-index,search,chat,evaluate,bias-audit,demo}
├── app/streamlit_app.py
├── scripts/build_sample_resumes.py
├── tests/               # 129 automated tests
├── data/{sample,raw}/   # synthetic sample; real Kaggle file goes in raw/ (git-ignored)
├── docs/                # METHODOLOGY · DATASET · LLM_SETUP · BIAS_AND_PRIVACY
├── notebooks/           # 01 offline walkthrough · 02 Colab with real models
├── outputs/demo/        # smoke-test outputs
├── .github/workflows/ci.yml
└── pyproject.toml · Makefile · LICENSE · CITATION.cff
```

## Fairness and privacy
Employment screening is a **high-risk** AI use: this project reduces risk (redaction, anonymous candidates to the LLM, grounded explanations, an audit) but does not remove it.
Use it to **shortlist and explain**, keep a human decision-maker, prefer a **local** LLM for real candidate data, and read [`docs/BIAS_AND_PRIVACY.md`](docs/BIAS_AND_PRIVACY.md)
(limits of the audit, proxies such as college or location, consent and retention). The raw Kaggle resumes are git-ignored - never commit personal data.

## Troubleshooting
* **`Resume data not found`** - see [`docs/DATASET.md`](docs/DATASET.md); pass `--data "<your file>"` if the file name differs.
* **`No index found`** - run `python -m talent_rag demo` or `build-index` first (the index is git-ignored).
* **LLM errors** - the CLI/UI falls back to the template explainer and shows the reason; check keys / model names / that `ollama serve` is running.
* **`pip install` is heavy** - use `".[faiss]"` only and `--embedder lsa --store faiss` (no torch, no chroma needed).
* **ChromaDB / FAISS missing** - install the extra (`pip install ".[chroma]"` / `".[faiss]"`) or use `--store numpy`.
* Indexes contain a pickle (`lsa.joblib`) - only load indexes you built yourself.

